module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.unresolved_name_is_reported_as_a_decidability_verdict

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data unresolved_name_is_reported_as_a_decidability_verdict: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "unresolved_name_is_reported_as_a_decidability_verdict" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**an unresolved name is reported as a decidability verdict, and at the blocking end as a TYPE** (INVALID STATE: a reference that failed to resolve is reported in a category that presupposes it resolved -- as an undecidable position, or as a type spelled with the unresolved name -- so the report is true-sounding and the resolution deficit is destroyed at the point of reporting). ",

    "HARM, AND IT HAS TWO ENDS THAT ARE THE SAME MECHANISM. The advisory end WIDENS: the arm cannot compute the precise answer -- this name does not resolve -- so it substitutes a wider one that is honestly true of some positions, that the position may be undecidable. Nothing is fabricated, which is exactly why it reads as diligent. The blocking end FABRICATES: an unresolved callee's AUTHORED NAME becomes a type in a type-equality verdict, so the compiler states that two branches have incompatible types where one of the two is not a type at all but the spelling of a function it failed to look up. That is a false statement about the program, which section 5 forbids outright as fabricated plausible output, and it sits below the section 4b floor, where values inhabiting declared types is baseline rather than differentiator. ",

    "**MEASURED, AND THE INSTRUMENT IS NAMED RATHER THAN ITS OUTPUT TRANSCRIBED.** The producer is the whole-corpus compile `gunbc compile --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --source-root src/v1 --target dag`, whose advisory stream carries the reason spelling; the counted class is the advisories whose reason is `generic formal`, and the neighbouring reasons on the same stream -- among them `optional carrier` -- are the invariant controls. The design is a controlled A/B: the SAME invocation on both arms, a binary built at each side, one corpus; arm A is the tree where the references resolve, arm B the tree where a supply change stops a class of references resolving. Re-deriving is counting that reason on each arm. ",

    "WHAT THAT A/B SHOWS, STATED AS THE CLAIM THE INSTRUMENT DECIDES RATHER THAN AS A FIGURE. The `generic formal` population is small on arm A and larger by orders of magnitude on arm B, while the neighbouring reasons do not move -- and every instance the second arm adds is a name that did not resolve. The invariance of the neighbours is what makes this a mechanism rather than a coincidence, so a re-derivation that moved them too would REFUTE this row rather than confirm it. An earlier draft of this receipt carried the two counts as literals; they are removed because a transcribed number is unreachable from the producer that owns it, and this row is the specimen -- the figures could no longer be re-derived from the run artifacts that produced them, which is the decay DESIGN section 6 names, observed on this row's own evidence. ",

    "**THE CONCEALMENT IS WHY THIS IS STRUCTURAL AND NOT A WORDING DEFECT.** The honest arm for an unresolved formal EXISTS -- it is spelled UndecidableFormalUnresolved -- AND IT FIRED ZERO TIMES IN BOTH ARMS OF THE A/B. It cannot fire, because the name it tests is read from the AUTHORED SOURCE rather than from resolution: the authored spelling survives a failed lookup, so the formal never looks unresolved, and the next arm in the chain -- a type variable in the inferred slot -- is reached instead and reports the position as generic. A specimen names the falseness exactly: the declared parameter type is a product type declared with NO parameters, so `generic formal` is not imprecise about it, it is false about it. ",

    "**WHY NOBODY LOOKED, WHICH IS THE TRANSFERABLE PART.** The defect was never hidden. It was REPORTED, in a category that reads as honest, at a population small enough that no one had reason to examine it. It became visible only when an unrelated change multiplied the population by a hundred, and it was PRE-EXISTING throughout -- the change made it loud, it did not cause it. So the recognition rule is not `look for missing diagnostics`: it is that a diagnostic category which is HONESTLY TRUE OF SOME POPULATION will absorb a failure it was not written for, and absorption is invisible in proportion to how plausible the category is. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: a failure arm that answers a WIDER TRUE THING when it cannot compute the precise one -- the absorbing fallback of section 5, here at the DIAGNOSTIC layer rather than at an execution boundary. The mechanical tells: an honest arm that exists and never fires; a verdict that presupposes the very resolution that failed; and a category whose population moves by orders of magnitude under a change that should not have touched it. Its ceiling is structural -- a diagnostic may not name a category whose precondition is unestablished, which is decidable from the resolution result already in hand -- and the next-rung trigger is that the unresolved case be constructed rather than inferred: the reason arm chosen from the RESOLUTION OUTCOME rather than from an authored name that outlives the failure. ",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
